From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:58:34 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: reboot-mode: Handle zero-valued mode magic

The original 2016 binding required nonzero mode values, and the YAML
conversion retained that rule even though its normal-mode example uses
zero. Correct the binding first, then distinguish a configured zero from
an unknown command instead of using the magic as a found flag.

This changes da850-lego-ev3: its mode-normal = <0> is now written on a
plain reboot, as its DT requests. Unmatched commands still leave the
marker alone. Google Tensor also needs explicit zero: the GPL Pixel
reset driver defines REBOOT_MODE_NORMAL as zero in SYSIP_DAT0 and writes
it for from_fastboot, shell and userrequested commands. Skipping zero
can leave a prior bootloader request in place.

Return the matched mode descriptor and let the notifier write its magic.
Keep command normalization and write-callback handling unchanged. The
actual lookup and notifier pass 21 source-extracted behavioral cases,
including zero/nonzero modes, unknown commands, aliases, long names and
write errors. The old code reproduces the zero normal-mode failure.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/power/reset/+/ae088532b5e965536723b6b649b42a5b90717287/pixel-zuma-reboot.c
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c | 20 ++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
index 3611bed34..b221c4215 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
@@ -72,8 +72,8 @@ static const struct class reboot_mode_class = {
 	.dev_groups = reboot_mode_groups,
 };
 
-static unsigned int get_reboot_mode_magic(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
-					  const char *cmd)
+static const struct mode_info *get_reboot_mode(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
+					       const char *cmd)
 {
 	const char *normal = "normal";
 	struct mode_info *info;
@@ -84,11 +84,11 @@ static unsigned int get_reboot_mode_magic(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
 
 	list_for_each_entry(info, &reboot->head, list)
 		if (!strcmp(info->mode, cmd))
-			return info->magic;
+			return info;
 
 	/* try to match again, replacing characters impossible in DT */
 	if (strscpy(cmd_, cmd, sizeof(cmd_)) == -E2BIG)
-		return 0;
+		return NULL;
 
 	strreplace(cmd_, ' ', '-');
 	strreplace(cmd_, ',', '-');
@@ -96,21 +96,21 @@ static unsigned int get_reboot_mode_magic(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
 
 	list_for_each_entry(info, &reboot->head, list)
 		if (!strcmp(info->mode, cmd_))
-			return info->magic;
+			return info;
 
-	return 0;
+	return NULL;
 }
 
 static int reboot_mode_notify(struct notifier_block *this,
 			      unsigned long mode, void *cmd)
 {
 	struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot;
-	unsigned int magic;
+	const struct mode_info *info;
 
 	reboot = container_of(this, struct reboot_mode_driver, reboot_notifier);
-	magic = get_reboot_mode_magic(reboot, cmd);
-	if (magic)
-		reboot->write(reboot, magic);
+	info = get_reboot_mode(reboot, cmd);
+	if (info)
+		reboot->write(reboot, info->magic);
 
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
 }
